{"id": "ebed03b6-c9a4-4fe8-9352-9266816541b6", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'm realizing that this "dr-demo-vault-dr" backup vault in eu-west-1 is actually the DR target for a separate "dr-demo" workload whose primary region is eu-central-1, where the RDS instance and DynamoDB table originate before being cross-region copied into eu-west-1.

So none of the eu-west-1-native production workloads (orders-web, booking-api, telemetry, catalog-eks) actually have any backup plan or cross-region copy configured for themselves — eu-west-1 only serves as a DR destination for the unrelated eu-central-1 workload, not the reverse. I'll note this as a tangential finding and move on to compiling the final report.

